# Java

Follow skills **java** and **poteto-java** when applicable.

- Formatter clean (google-java-format or Spotless; spring-javaformat accepted)
- Checkstyle or Error Prone wired where practical
- Nullability contracts (jspecify / NullMarked / NullAway / Checker / Spring Nullable)
- No `System.out` / `System.err` print without `java-rg-allow` + rationale; prefer a logger
- No `printStackTrace` without `java-rg-allow` + rationale; prefer a logger
- No SQL/string concat without `java-rg-allow` + rationale; prefer `PreparedStatement`
- No `catch (NullPointerException` without `java-rg-allow` + rationale; fix nullable contracts
- Required product gates: `java-rg-gate` + `java-hotpath-gate` + `java-fmt-gate` + `java-checkstyle-ci-gate` + `java-nullability-gate`. Do not disable checks to force green.
- Prove runtime behaviour with tests / Checkstyle / Error Prone, not "fmt pass" alone

Repeated review smell twice on a Java product: encode into lint/CI/skill, not more prose.
